            <ArticleTitle>Multimodality plaque ablation following failure of conventional wires and balloons to cross and to allow successful paclitaxel-eluting stent implantation of a chronic total occlusion.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E7-10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Chronic total occlusion (CTO) is one of the most challenging coronary lesions to be faced in the catheterization laboratory. This report of a patient with stable angina and a CTO illustrates the potential problems that may arise and must be overcome, and demonstrates the utilization of technologies including the Intraluminal wire.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
